Slifer the Sky Dragon.

244
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,780
The Winged Dragon of Ra.

245
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:15,397
Ah, control one, and you can destroy
a million armies, wield all three,

246
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:17,892
and the planet itself will quake in fear.

247
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,717
And Pegasus turned them into cards?

248
00:16:19,800 --> 00:16:20,680
Yes. You lie.

249
00:16:20,920 --> 00:16:24,217
If he had them, why didn't he use
them against me at Duelist Kingdom?

250
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:27,888
Because Pegasus feared the power
of these Egyptian god cards.

251
00:16:28,140 --> 00:16:31,420
You cannot fathom the magical
energy contained within.

252
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:35,257
Pegasus could not control the
power of the cards he created.

253
00:16:35,340 --> 00:16:38,157
They threatened to
overwhelm and destroy him.

254
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:40,997
Cards that even make
Pegasus quake in his boots.

255
00:16:41,080 --> 00:16:45,457
If I can obtain the three legendary
monsters, I'll be unstoppable in any duel.

256
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,069
Yugi won't stand a chance.

257
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,377
But how do I get them?

258
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:49,760
I can't ask Pegasus.

259
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:51,497
He's dropped off the face of the Earth.

260
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:53,286
They have to exist somewhere.

261
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:57,160
Mishizu, what did Pegasus
do with the cards?

262
00:16:58,380 --> 00:17:00,780
He gave them to me for safekeeping.

263
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:06,777
Pegasus realized that if these
cards fell into the wrong hands,

264
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:08,977
they could bring about
the end of the world.

265
00:17:09,060 --> 00:17:12,997
He had me bury them in secret locations,
but the cards were discovered.

266
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,551
I must find them and hide them once again.

267
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:20,900
You mean someone already
found the cards? Yes.

268
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:22,060
Tell me who.

269
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:23,660
The Rare Hunters.

270
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:25,140
Rare Hunters?

271
00:17:25,560 --> 00:17:28,537
They're a ruthless underground
sect of elite duelists.

272
00:17:28,620 --> 00:17:31,957
They rob and steal rare cards worldwide to

273
00:17:32,040 --> 00:17:35,300
sell on the black market for
enormous profits. However,

274
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,957
they keep the strongest
cards for themselves to

275
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:41,060
create powerful decks that
destroy all opposition.

276
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:45,357
They operate in shadow, so they
are nearly impossible to find.

277
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:48,969
That is why I need your help
to draw them out into the open.

278
00:17:49,840 --> 00:17:52,817
Kaiba, if you were to start
a Duel Monsters tournament,

279
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:55,937
your reputation would attract the
greatest duelists in the world.

280
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:58,377
This would be the
greatest concentration of

281
00:17:58,460 --> 00:18:01,166
precious cards ever
assembled in one location.

282
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:02,830
I see.

283
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:03,920
It's a trap.

284
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:07,657
The rare hunters won't be able
to resist such tempting bait.

285
00:18:07,740 --> 00:18:11,180
They'll come by the droves,
like vultures to a carcass.

286
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:14,060
And they'll bring the Egyptian god cards.

287
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:17,200
One last thing.

288
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:18,800
Take this card.

289
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,840
Hmm? Can it be?

290
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:23,580
It's Obelisk the Tormentor!

291
00:18:23,820 --> 00:18:25,357
I thought the cards were stolen!

292
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,377
I never said they were all stolen.

293
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:29,460
I managed to retrieve one in time.

294
00:18:29,640 --> 00:18:32,497
You may borrow it during the
tournament, but I expect it back.

295
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:35,617
It's not every day a card
this rare is handed to me.

296
00:18:35,700 --> 00:18:37,759
What if I chose to keep it forever?

297
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,435
What makes you think I can be trusted?

298
00:18:40,540 --> 00:18:43,246
I could walk out and
you'd never see it again.

299
00:18:44,880 --> 00:18:46,800
You will return the card to me.

300
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,560
I have foreseen it.

301
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,130
I'll bet.

302
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:57,617
You may not yet believe in destiny,
but before the tournament is done,

303
00:18:57,700 --> 00:18:59,960
you will have to face your past.

304
00:19:00,820 --> 00:19:03,585
You know, I read that
once in a fortune cookie.

305
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,580
I'll organize this
tournament. I thank you.

306
00:19:08,060 --> 00:19:10,317
But I'm not going to set
it up because of your

307
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:13,047
fairy tales and your
hocus-pocus mind tricks.

308
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:16,418
I want to reclaim my title
as the number one duelist.

309
00:19:18,520 --> 00:19:20,677
I wish we knew more about our new enemy.

310
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:25,020
He said he was familiar with
the power of a Millennium Item.

311
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:26,760
I bet he has one.

312
00:19:26,940 --> 00:19:29,528
That must be how he
controls people's minds.

313
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:32,836
It also seems he has knowledge
of the ancient customs.

314
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:35,600
Our foe is somehow connected to the past.

315
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:37,960
But who is he? I don't know.

316
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,691
Then how can we stop him?

317
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:44,450
Don't worry.

318
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,621
We can defeat this evil together.

319
00:19:47,780 --> 00:19:51,192
As long as we stay connected,
you and I can face anything.

320
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:54,820
Maybe, but what if I fail again?

321
00:19:55,720 --> 00:19:57,838
How do I know that I won't lose you?

322
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:02,600
I believe in you, Yugi.

323
00:20:12,960 --> 00:20:16,480
One car down and two more to go
